[[ ========================================
SKETCH ENGINE
======================================== ]]

[[ NORMAL WORLD:
What is happening before anything becomes funny?
Keep the set-up fast and active.
]]

[[ COMIC PREMISE:
What is slightly wrong?
]]

[[ TRIGGER:
What repeatable event causes the build-up?
]]

[[ AUDIENCE ANTICIPATION:
What does the audience understand is going to happen?
]]

[[ ========================================
FIVE STEPS TO HEAVEN
======================================== ]]

[[ STEP 1 — AUDIENCE KNOWS
Trigger occurs.
The characters do not react.
The audience recognizes its significance.
]]

[[ STEP 2 — THEY NOTICE
Trigger repeats.
Characters register it but continue what they're doing.
]]

[[ STEP 3 — ACTION CHANGES
Trigger.
FIXED POINT.
Resume action with increased intensity / changed behavior.
]]

[[ STEP 4 — TENSION TAKES OVER
Trigger.
FIXED POINT.
Continue the established action, but the tension is now
visibly affecting the characters.
]]

[[ STEP 5 — ORDER BREAKS DOWN
Trigger.
Longest FIXED POINT.
Release into panic / ecstasy / fantasy / chaos /
whatever extreme belongs to this world.
]]

[[ PAYOFF / CHANGE OF FEELING:
What changes?
Don't merely make Step 4 louder.
]]

INT. LOCATION - DAY

Action begins.